add('Background and motivation',body=c('Professor LUO RUIBANG asked who would completely trust AI.','I raised my hand because I use different agents to cross-check.','Does an extra check actually make the answer more reliable?'),takeaway='Our confidence in cross-checking is the hypothesis we test.',foot='Paraphrased from LINYUNIAN’s recollection of the class.',notes='Tell the classroom story in the first person. The professor wording is a recollection, not an independently verified verbatim quotation. Move from a personal reason for trusting AI to a testable research question.',sources=c(feishu,paste0(readme,'CHAT_CONTEXT.md#u31')),seconds=55)
add('Research questions',layout='questions',body=c('1. Can double-checking reduce AI error rates?','2. Which double-checking method is most effective in practice?','3. Can an incorrect peer answer mislead an initially correct model during cross-checking?','4. Can misleading user input cause an otherwise correct model to give a wrong answer?'),notes='Use the four questions exactly as in the Feishu document. RQ1 asks about a net reduction; RQ2 compares methods; RQ3 conditions on a correct receiver and wrong peer; RQ4 tests misleading user input to the same model.',sources=feishu,seconds=45)
